-> Range constraints narrow a variable's domain.
a > 5
a < 12

-> After narrowing, the domain is (5, 12) — no concrete value yet,
-> but assertions on domain bounds should hold.
-> For now, range-constrained vars without an exact value are not
-> directly readable, so we constrain then pin:
b = 7
b > 5
b < 12
assert b = 7

-> GreaterEqual / LessEqual
c = 10
c ≥ 5
c ≤ 15
assert c = 10

-> Single-sided range
d = 100
d > 0
assert d = 100

e = 0 - 3
e < 0
assert e = 0 - 3
